# Frontend Development Guidelines

## Empty States and User Feedback

When implementing empty states (no data scenarios), follow these principles to avoid distracting users:

### 1. Avoid Alert Boxes
Don't use `alert alert-info` or similar Bootstrap alert classes for empty states. These are too visually prominent and distracting.

### 2. Use Subtle Visual Design
- Muted gray text colors (`color: var(--gray-500)` or `#6b7280`)
- Icons with low opacity (`opacity: 0.3`)
- No background colors or borders
- Centered text alignment
- Adequate padding for breathing room

### 3. Empty State Pattern

```html
<!-- Good: Subtle empty state -->
<div class="empty-state">
    <i class="bi bi-calendar-check"></i>
    <p>No events scheduled for this day</p>
    <a href="{% url 'event_create' %}" class="btn btn-primary">Create Event</a>
</div>

<!-- Bad: Distracting alert box -->
<div class="alert alert-info">
    No events scheduled for this day.
</div>
```

### 4. CSS for Empty States

```css
.empty-state {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 3rem 2rem;
    color: var(--gray-500);
}

.empty-state > i {
    font-size: 3rem;
    opacity: 0.3;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    display: block;
}

.empty-state h4 {
    color: var(--gray-600);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}

.empty-state p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
}
```

### 5. Loading States
When loading data asynchronously, show a loading spinner first, then transition to either the data or empty state without jarring visual changes.

Example:
```javascript
function renderMediaGallery() {
    if (mediaItems.length === 0) {
        mediaContainer.innerHTML = `
            <div class="text-center text-muted py-4">
                <i class="bi bi-image" style="font-size: 3rem; opacity: 0.3;"></i>
                <p class="mt-2 mb-0">No photos or videos have been added yet</p>
            </div>
        `;
        return;
    }
    // ... render actual content
}
```

## Alert Messages

### Django Messages
- System messages (login success, errors, etc.) should auto-dismiss after 5 seconds
- Position: Fixed position in top-right corner, sliding in from the right
- Visual Design: Use subtle shadows and slide animations, not harsh borders or bright backgrounds

### CSS Variables
The application uses CSS variables defined in `main.css`. Use these for consistency:
- `--gray-500`: #6b7280 (muted text)
- `--gray-600`: #4b5563 (slightly darker text)
- `--space-*`: Consistent spacing values
- `--radius-*`: Consistent border radius values

## Icons
The application uses Bootstrap Icons. Common icons for empty states:
- `bi-calendar-check`: No events
- `bi-calendar-x`: No scheduled items
- `bi-image`: No photos/media
- `bi-calendar-plus`: Add new event/vacation

